Package: aqlyzer
Title: Fluorescence Kinetics Analysis for Microplate Assays
Version: 0.99.0
Date: 2026-07-01
Authors@R: 
    person(c("Ali", "Sajid"), "Imami", , "Ali.Sajid.Imami@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-3684-3539"))
Description: Provides a reproducible pipeline for processing and analysing
    time-resolved fluorescence kinetics data from 96-well plate readers.
    Covers plate layout validation, signal preprocessing (zeroing, blank
    subtraction, replicate averaging), automated linear range detection,
    and linear model fitting for per-sample parameter extraction.
    Linear range detection is implemented in Rust via extendr for
    performance, with a pure R fallback. A Shiny application is included
    for push-button analysis without direct use of R code.
